# Mini-Zork I (minizork.z3) benchmark script — SQ-1428.
#
# One command per line; blank lines and lines starting with '#' are skipped
# by `cargo run -p lanthorn-zvm --example bench` and must be stripped before
# the same script is fed to dfrotz (see ../README.md for the exact command).
#
# Eight commands that leave the game exactly where they found it: the
# above-ground house circuit (north/east/south/west returns to West of House)
# plus four parser-only turns. Every command is idempotent on repetition —
# `open mailbox` answers "It is already open.", `take leaflet` answers "You
# already have that." — so the cycle can be looped for tens of thousands of
# turns without the game ending, dying, or drifting into a different state.
# Nothing here reaches the Thief, the grue, the lamp battery or any random
# event; the score stays 0 and the only counter that moves is Moves.
open mailbox
take leaflet
read leaflet
north
east
south
west
inventory
